# Public posts: mask personal data

`maroomir/storyboard` is public. Issues, PRs, comments, releases, commit messages, fixtures and docs
must never carry personal data — an edited post keeps the original in its edit history.

- Notion ids (32 hex or dashed UUID) and Notion URLs carrying one → `https://www.notion.so/<id>`, `'<Notion 페이지 URL>'`.
- Personal links (`*.notion.site`, vault paths, private document links) → `<개인 링크>`.
- Home paths (`/Users/<name>/…`, `/home/<name>/…`) → `~/…`, `/path/to/workspace`.
- Tokens (`ntn_…`, `secret_…`, `sk-…`, `ghp_…`) → `<token>`; other people's e-mails → `<email>`.
- Repro commands keep their shape and lose their values.
- Check before posting: `grep -nE '[0-9a-f]{32}|notion\.(so|site|com)/|/Users/|/home/' body.md` prints only placeholders.
- If something leaked, edit the post and delete the old revision from its edit history on GitHub's web UI.

Canonical rule: `.claude/rules/public-posts.md` (Claude Code also enforces it with a PreToolUse hook).
